     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Shiny app, which is automaticly generated by rstudio when you click (file &gt; new file &gt; shiny web app) doesn&#39;t work, turns to gray screen on chrome and rstudio crushes.</div><div><br></div><div>How I noticed this is, my own app crushed when I try to add output of a ggplot chart. This template has a basic histogram, I guess the problem is about plots.</div><div><br></div><div>**I only copy and paste template here**</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This is a Shiny web application. You can run the application by clicking</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># the &#39;Run App&#39; button above.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Find out more about building applications with Shiny here:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#    <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389491069000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1eVUlZSTsU-F4dc-RpysiR\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/</a></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Define UI for application that draws a histogram</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ui </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fluidPage</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   <br>   </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Application title</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   titlePanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Old Faithful Geyser Data&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   <br>   </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Sidebar with a slider input for number of bins </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   sidebarLayout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      sidebarPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         sliderInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bins&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Number of bins:&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     min </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     max </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     value </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      <br>      </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Show a plot of the generated distribution</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      mainPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         plotOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;distPlot&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Define server logic required to draw a histogram</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>server </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   <br>   output$distPlot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderPlot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># generate bins based on input$bins from ui.R</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      x    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> faithful</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>      bins </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$bins </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      <br>      </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># draw the histogram with the specified number of bins</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      hist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> breaks </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bins</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;darkgray&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> border </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;white&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Run the application </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>shinyApp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ui </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ui</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> server </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> server</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div></div><div>**my session info** </div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><cod